From 8bcca206718706cbbe553613501d8437c2bb65f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Skip multiArch ABI forceMatch for system apps

Android 15+ (VANILLA_ICE_CREAM) introduced a forceMatch check in
derivePackageAbi that rejects multiArch apps targeting SDK 35+ if
they lack native libs for every ABI the device supports. This
causes system apps like Vanadium (which ships 64-bit only) to be
silently rejected during boot scan on multilib devices that
advertise 32-bit ABI support via the vendor partition.

Skip the forceMatch check for system apps since their ABI
configuration is intentional and controlled by the ROM builder.
Third-party app installs still get the full check.
---
 .../core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java  | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java
index 639d02ca4..ccc234655 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java
@@ -386,7 +386,8 @@ final class PackageAbiHelperImpl implements PackageAbiHelper {
                 // Force the match for these cases
                 // 1. pkg.getTargetSdkVersion >= Build.VERSION_CODES.VANILLA_ICE_CREAM
                 // 2. cpuAbiOverride is null. If it is non-null, it is set via shell for testing
-                final boolean forceMatch =
+                // 3. Not a system app (system apps are controlled by the ROM builder)
+                final boolean forceMatch = !isSystemApp &&
                         pkg.getTargetSdkVersion() >= Build.VERSION_CODES.VANILLA_ICE_CREAM
                         && cpuAbiOverride == null;

